# Berlin AutoWorks — Project Rules

This is a modular monolith Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript application for a fictional auto repair shop.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router (src/app/) with TypeScript (strict)
- Server Components by default
- Prisma + PostgreSQL
- Redis + BullMQ (or equivalent) for jobs/caching
- Stripe (or equivalent) for payments — never store card data
- Auth.js / NextAuth (or Clerk/Auth0)
- Tailwind CSS + accessible primitives (Radix-based preferred)

## Architecture
- Three surfaces in one codebase:
  - Public marketing (`/`)
  - Customer portal (`/account/**`)
  - Staff workspace (`/admin/**`)
- Domain modules (in-process): identity, locations, catalog, scheduling, estimates, repairs, billing, customers, notifications, audit, files
- Every transactional record must carry `locationId` (multi-location ready)
- Launch is single-location; do not hard-code a single shop

## Hard Rules
- Prefer Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when necessary (interactivity, browser APIs, payment elements).
- Never use the Pages Router.
- No `any` types. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- Validate all inputs with Zod.
- Customer and admin routes must be dynamic, uncached (`Cache-Control: private, no-store`), and noindex.
- Public marketing pages prefer ISR.
- Run typecheck + lint before considering a task complete.
- Card data never touches application servers.
- Internal notes and non-customer-visible photos must never appear in the customer portal.
